 "intro_html": "Momofuku’s ginger scallion sauce is just scallions, ginger, oil and a little seasoning stirred together raw — and their amount of ginger is <b>hot and hard on the palate</b>. This version keeps the idea but makes it softer: <b>half the ginger</b>, a bit <b>more scallion and oil</b>, the oil <b>poured over hot</b> to mellow the raw ginger, and a pinch of sugar and a drop of sesame oil to round it off. Best with the <a href=\"alkaline-ramen-noodles.html\">baked-soda ramen noodles</a>.",
