 "notes": [
  {
   "html": "<ul class=\"do\"><li>Momofuku’s original, stirred together raw:<ul class=\"ing two-col\"><li><span class=\"q\" data-k=\"vol\" data-u=\"cup\" data-a=\"2.5\" data-s=\"0\">2½ cups</span> sliced scallions</li><li><span class=\"q\" data-k=\"vol\" data-u=\"cup\" data-a=\"0.5\" data-s=\"0\">½ cup</span> minced ginger</li><li><span class=\"q\" data-k=\"vol\" data-u=\"cup\" data-a=\"0.3333\" data-s=\"0\">⅓ cup</span> grapeseed oil</li><li><span class=\"q\" data-k=\"vol\" data-u=\"tsp\" data-a=\"1.5\" data-s=\"0\">1½ tsp</span> usukuchi</li><li><span class=\"q\" data-k=\"vol\" data-u=\"tsp\" data-a=\"0.75\" data-s=\"0\">¾ tsp</span> sherry vinegar</li><li><span class=\"q\" data-k=\"vol\" data-u=\"tsp\" data-a=\"0.75\" data-s=\"0\">¾ tsp</span> kosher salt</li></ul></li><li>This version:<ul class=\"ing two-col\"><li>ginger halved to <span class=\"q\" data-k=\"vol\" data-u=\"cup\" data-a=\"0.25\" data-s=\"0\">¼ cup</span>, minced finer</li><li>scallions up to <span class=\"q\" data-k=\"vol\" data-u=\"cup\" data-a=\"3\" data-s=\"0\">3 cups</span></li><li>oil up to <span class=\"q\" data-k=\"vol\" data-u=\"cup\" data-a=\"0.5\" data-s=\"0\">½ cup</span>, poured over hot</li><li>soy up to <span class=\"q\" data-k=\"vol\" data-u=\"tsp\" data-a=\"2\" data-s=\"0\">2 tsp</span>, salt down to <span class=\"q\" data-k=\"vol\" data-u=\"tsp\" data-a=\"0.5\" data-s=\"0\">½ tsp</span></li><li>added: <span class=\"q\" data-k=\"vol\" data-u=\"tsp\" data-a=\"1\" data-s=\"0\">1 tsp</span> sugar and <span class=\"q\" data-k=\"vol\" data-u=\"tsp\" data-a=\"0.5\" data-s=\"0\">½ tsp</span> toasted sesame oil</li></ul></li></ul>",
   "title_html": "Original vs this version"
  },
  {
   "html": "<ul class=\"do\"><li>Cut the ginger to 2 tablespoons.</li><li>Blanch the minced ginger in boiling water for 30 seconds and drain it before the hot oil goes on.</li><li>Let the sauce sit an hour before using — it keeps mellowing.</li><li>Add more scallion rather than more seasoning.</li></ul>",
   "title_html": "If it’s still too sharp"
  },
  {
   "html": "<ul class=\"do\"><li>Momofuku serves these with quick pickles, pan-roasted cauliflower, bamboo shoots and nori.</li><li>The <a href=\"cucumber-sunomono.html\">cucumber pickle</a> works well as the pickle.</li></ul>",
   "title_html": "Toppings"
  },
  {
   "html": "<p>Adapted from Momofuku’s ginger scallion noodles (David Chang and Peter Meehan, <i>Momofuku</i>, 2009), made gentler and written in my own words.</p>",
   "title_html": "Based on"
  }
 ],
